<title>BELGIUM: Belgian money market supply raised in week.</title>
<headline>Belgian money market supply raised in week.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian central bank said it added liquidity to the money market in the week to March 3 in order to counter the liquidity-boosting effect of a rise in note circulation.</p>
<p>(figures from the weekly statement in bln francs) -</p>
<p> Foreign currency reserves	   447.46 (+  1.35)</p>
<p> Advances against pledged security  14.74 (-  2.70)</p>
<p> Commercial bills			  2.62 (unchanged)</p>
<p> Securities portfolio		   21.34 (-  0.50)</p>
<p> Money market interventions*	  93.71 (+  4.88)</p>
<p> Bank notes in circulation	   449.08 (+  1.37)</p>
<p>* comprises repurchase agreements and interbank loans</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
